hese so yeah  we definitely get some nice air time  there then into a zero g roll and then  finally an immelmann turn to turn back  to another airtime hill  and finally into the station so  really it is a pretty short ride to be  honest  uh just an imminent into an air time  into zero zero immediate air time so not  too much is going on but i really had  quite a tight space to work with here  and i think  given just how little space it takes up  in the park especially because it's kind  of toward the edges on space that you  know it's not really using anything that  could be used very differently  i think it's a it's a very nice  compromise to get a launched coaster in  here with still some decent elements  and a decent mix and variety of elements  as well so that's the launched coaster  now for the b m floorless i think i'm  just gonna  let this one go back to the station and  see if we can catch the next ride when  it's actually fixed well let's see if  we've got any  uh mechanics coming up to this one all  right so there's our mechanic he's just  gonna have to go through the staircase  in the middle of the building here and  then we can actually follow the path as  it goes up to the coaster so there's a  little bit of uh going around there then  into the uh exit there which is this  whole covert section here and then  hopefully the people can get on and we  can get on and we can do a quick pov of  this ride so  we've really got this interesting setup  here with all of the different parts  going over and under each other and kind  of intertwining here it's very hard to  tell what's going on  unless you turn on the buildings which  i'll do in a second but yeah first  a pov of this coaster  given how tight this thing is it kind of  reminds me of daymonen at tivoli which  is  a layout which i find really impressive  especially given the fact that it's real  life you know but this one is a little  bit crazier we start off going into that  immelmann then into kind of bizarre  elements into a cobra roll  it's really weird but it just works on a  very tight space and you know we already  have four inversions going into this  very compact layout then some turns  going around which is kind of typical i  suppose for the latter half of a b m  coaster into this zero g raw  barrel roll kind of thing it really does  have some interaction with the path here  a bit of a literal head chopper at the  end there and some of the buildings that  could presumably be you know the  transfer track and all of that jazz but  i decided to you know pass on that one  but there's still some interesting stuff  going on here if we turn off the  buildings you can see some of the part  work that's actually in here this giant  kind of staircase and then the  intermingling paths here with over here  the uh pretty large  uh q line for the orbiter which is also  a very popular ride i'm kind of blown  away just by how popular this thing is  uh but let's turn the buildings back on  that definitely looks a bit better  and over here we have the  still turned off right  uh that's such a classic why do i always  always make that mistake with at least  one of my flat rides in my park  i just realized i basically could have  done without this thing because i've  reached the goals anyway but it just it  just looks too good on that position and  it just looks too good as a flat ride in  general  i don't know why everything is breaking  down but we'll continue the tour so we  have the tool beyond here  doing its thing looking absolutely nuts  i  really want to write one of these things  even though i've heard they're not quite  as interesting to ride as they are to  look at i think they're definitely one  of the most interesting and creative  flat right designs in real life then  we've got the jumper here and the food  stuffs i couldn't really come up with a  better name for some of the food stuff  it's not very good food stuffs by the  way i decided to go with some bubble tea  because we are in an asian map after all  and bubble tea is from taiwan if i  remember correctly but  the general culture plus you can  definitely find it in tokyo as well  and then we have a vending machine for  food which might be the reason that  my hunger rating is not quite that good  definitely something to keep in mind  once you get one of these scenarios  where you start off without a proper  food stall you can use the vending  machine chips to have people stave off  the hunger for the most part but  obviously it's not very healthy with all  of that salt and sunflower oil but you  know it's uh  whoops it's it's something that that  kind of works in a pinch i suppose but  next time i should definitely research a  proper food stall as well here we have  the riptide no longer smashing speakers  heads into the ceiling so that's nice  and  another flat ride hidden in here and in  here as well so all things considered i  think there's a lot of stuff going on in  this map but just enough not to make it  feel too crammed and definitely once you  turn off the scenery you can tell how  everything actually works and you can  see that there's a lot of path space  just kind of hidden everywhere just to  make sure that this park doesn't get too  crammed despite the fact that the  footprint that we have to work with is  very small in this one  oh and before i forget i do usually want  to try to cover the ratings but i always  forget to do this but the ratings on the  coasters are pretty good we've got 82  excitement and extreme excitement on  this one and decently medium intensity  and nausea and on this one it's just  very high so not quite as good it's not  quite as intense um but still i think a  decent amount of variety had i a little  bit more space i definitely would have  included a junior coaster as well but  it's really hard to make those things  actually fit into a compact space  ironically enough i think it's easier to  build a little bit larger and built a 